'''''The Old Republic — The Lost Suns'' 1''' is the seventh issue of the monthly comic [[Star Wars: The Old Republic (comic series)|''Star Wars: The Old Republic'' comic series]].

==Publisher's summary==
''The Lost Suns is set approximately 3,600 years before the movies. It stars Republic spy Theron Shan, son of Jedi Master Satele Shan, and packs explosive revelations relating to the events of the game''.

==Plot summary==
In exchange for credits, a vagrant tells about [[Syo Bakarn]], [[Bela Kiwiiks]], [[Jaric Kaedan]], and [[Satele Shan]] during the last days of the [[Great Galactic War]]. During the [[Battle of Rhen Var]], they led Republic troops against the [[Sith Empire (Post-Great Hyperspace War)|Empire]] while [[Unidentified Imperial commander (Rhen Var)|an Imperial commander]] told [[Darth Mekhis]] that the planet would be theirs. However, Shan kicked open the doors of her chamber and told her to surrender in exchange for being protected as a prisoner of war.

On [[Coruscant/Legends|Coruscant]], in [[3643 BBY]], while on a mission for the [[Republic Strategic Information Service]], [[Theron Shan]] captured the slaver [[Teff'ith]], planning on getting information, although she refused. The next morning, [[Director of Republic Strategic Information Service|Director]] [[Marcus Trant]] told Shan that a vagrant caught trespassing at an outpost near the Imperial border matched the description of [[Jedi Master/Legends|Jedi Master]] [[Ngani Zho]], who went missing after the war and trained half of the [[Jedi Council/Legends|Jedi Council]], including [[Grand Master/Legends|Grand Master]] Satele Shan, and that he claimed he was on his way back from the [[Vesla system/Legends|Vesla system]]. Because the system was ceded to the Empire in the [[Treaty of Coruscant]], Trant tasked Shan with rendezvousing with Zho and finding out everything he knew. When Teff'ith still refused to give Shan information, he told her that she would be coming with him to meet Zho. Elsewhere, Darth Mekhis planned to gift the [[Javelin (Harrower-class)|Javelin]] to [[Darth Marr]] and declared that her "true name" was "Ror'jhan". Then, she ordered [[Eisek]] to send her [[Darth Mekhis' Sith Knights|Sith Knights]] to find Zho.

